[Result "1/2-1/2"]
[WhiteElo "3036"]
[BlackElo "3027"]
[ECO "C00"]
[Opening "French Defense: St. George Defense"]

{French Defense: St. George Defense. Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.}
1. e4 a6 2. d4 e6 3. Be3 d5 4. Nd2 c5 5. dxc5 Nf6 {A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.} 6. a3 Nc6 7. b4 Be7 8. Bd3 ! a5 {A long think. Both continuations are playable; this one keeps more pieces on, which suits the attacker.} (8... d4 Rb1 dxe3 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. b5 Ne5 10. Ngf3 Neg4 11. Bd4 dxe4 ?! 12. Nxe4 e5 13. Bb2 Nxe4 14. Bxe4 Qxd1+ 15. Rxd1 Bxc5 16. O-O Nf6 17. Nd2 O-O 18. Bf3 Bg4 19. Nc4 Rac8 20. Bxe5 Bxf2+ 21. Rxf2 Rxc4 22. Bxf6 Bxf3 23. gxf3 gxf6 24. Rg2+ Kh8 25. Rd7 b6 26. Rb7 Ra4 27. h4 Rxa3 28. Rxb6 Ra1+ 29. Kh2 Ra4 30. Rg4 Ra2 31. Rc4 a4 32. Rxf6 a3 33. Ra6 Rg8 34. Rc5 Ra1 35. b6 Rb1 36. c4 a2 37. Rxa2 Rxb6 38. Rf5 Rd6 39. Rxf7 Rd4 40. Kh3 Rd1 41. Rf4 Rh1+ 42. Rh2 Rhg1 43. Rc2 Rh1+ 44. Rh2 Rf1 45. h5 {Precise to the end. A pawn move here instead would have let the defence build a fortress.} h6 1/2-1/2

